Critical iOS lifecycle/privacy overlay bug — screenshots and App Switcher are incorrectly blacking out BlueMind

I found a second iOS lifecycle issue on the real iPhone.

Current behavior:

1. When I take a screenshot while BlueMind is open, the app briefly becomes black / appears to reset or reload.
2. When I open the iOS App Switcher, BlueMind’s app preview/snapshot is completely black.

Other apps such as ChatGPT show their actual last visible screen in the App Switcher and taking a screenshot does not cause the app UI to black out or refresh.

I want BlueMind to behave normally.

⸻

TARGET BEHAVIOR

Screenshot

Taking a screenshot must NOT:

* cover the app with black;
* hide the root view;
* reload the React/Capacitor UI;
* reset navigation;
* trigger lock state;
* trigger privacy overlay;
* recreate the root controller.

The app should remain visually unchanged.

App Switcher

When BlueMind enters the iOS App Switcher:

* show the normal last rendered screen snapshot;
* do NOT replace it with a black view;
* do NOT hide the entire app window.

⸻

